        {
          "supplier": "thm-qsm-dt-choi-kraus",
          "carrier": "items/thm-qsm-dt-choi-kraus.md",
          "status": "Current carrier status: published; inspected for this dependency interface.",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Let $d,e\\geq1$ and let $\\Phi:M_d(\\mathbb C)\\to M_e(\\mathbb C)$ be complex-linear. Choose the standard input basis $(|i\\rangle)_{i=1}^d$, let $E_{ij}=|i\\rangle\\langle j|$, and use the ordered tensor convention input-reference $\\otimes$ output. Define the (unnormalized) Choi matrix\n\n$$J(\\Phi):=\\sum_{i,j=1}^{d}E_{ij}\\otimes\\Phi(E_{ij})\\in M_d(\\mathbb C)\\otimes M_e(\\mathbb C).$$ Then $\\Phi$ is completely positive if and only if $J(\\Phi)\\geq0$, and this holds if and only if there are $q\\leq de$ matrices $K_1,\\ldots,K_q:\\mathbb C^d\\to\\mathbb C^e$ such that $$\\Phi(X)=\\sum_{a=1}^{q}K_aXK_a^*\\qquad(X\\in M_d(\\mathbb C)).$$\n\nThe empty sum is allowed when $\\Phi=0$. For any such Kraus representation, $\\Phi$ is trace-preserving if and only if $\\sum_{a=1}^{q}K_a^*K_a=I_d$.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "The exact selected section above gives the interface; the consumer invokes it under its stated finite-dimensional hypotheses.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Supplier status is published; this carrier has no proof section, as appropriate to its kind. No independent approval is asserted.",
          "consumer_use": "Declared in the consumer reference interface; exact usage was inspected."
        }
      ],
      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "notes": "Checked each exact declared interface, its hypotheses and conventions, and its consuming use. This Step 1 record is not independent proof approval."
      },
      "repair_confidence": 1,
      "physics_review": {
        "formulation": {
          "verdict": "pass",
