          "status": "Current carrier status: published; inspected for this dependency interface.",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "The map $t\\mapsto(\\cos t,\\sin t)$ is a bijection from $[0,2\\pi)$ onto $S^1=\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x^2+y^2=1\\}$. The conventions and prerequisite facts used below are recorded in [[cor-trigonometric-parity-and-pythagorean-identity]], [[thm-sine-cosine-signs-monotonicity-and-ranges]], [[thm-sine-cosine-zero-sets-and-fundamental-period]], [[def-pi-via-first-positive-cosine-zero]].",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "Applicable consumer restatements: F3: [F3] [[thm-sine-and-cosine-parametrize-the-unit-circle]]: some $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)$ satisfies $(\\cos\\theta,\\sin\\theta)=(0,1)$.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Supplier status is published; this carrier has no proof section, as appropriate to its kind. No independent approval is asserted.",
          "consumer_use": "F3 is used in proof steps 1.2"
        }
      ],
