          "exact_statement": "Let $d\\geq1$, let $H=H^*\\in M_d(\\mathbb C)$ have units joules, let $\\hbar>0$ have units joule-seconds, and let $L_1,\\ldots,L_r\\in M_d(\\mathbb C)$ be a finite family with units $\\mathrm{s}^{-1/2}$, where $r\\geq0$. For the selected time-homogeneous finite GKSL model, put $\\mathcal L(X)=-\\frac{i}{\\hbar}[H,X]+\\sum_{a=1}^r(L_aXL_a^*-\\frac12\\{L_a^*L_a,X\\})$. With $K=-iH/\\hbar-\\frac12\\sum_aL_a^*L_a$ and the finite branch operators of [[def-nrqmx-finite-jump-trajectories]], each no-jump operator $R(u)=e^{uK}$ is a contraction, each branch state $W_{\\mathbf a,\\mathbf s}(t)\\rho W_{\\mathbf a,\\mathbf s}(t)^*$ is positive for $\\rho\\geq0$, and for every density matrix $\\rho$ and $t\\geq0$,\n\n$$e^{t\\mathcal L}(\\rho)=\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}\\ \\sum_{\\mathbf a\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}^n}\\ \\int_{0<s_1<\\cdots<s_n<t}W_{\\mathbf a,\\mathbf s}(t)\\rho W_{\\mathbf a,\\mathbf s}(t)^*\\,ds_1\\cdots ds_n,$$\n\nwhere the $n=0$ term is $R(t)\\rho R(t)^*$ and branches with $n\\geq1$ are absent when $r=0$. The series converges in trace norm, uniformly on each bounded time interval; the sum of all branch weights is one. This is an ensemble representation of the finite GKSL solution, not a unique microscopic trajectory or a claim about a particular detector.",
