          "exact_statement": "Let $d\\geq1$, let $r\\geq0$ be an integer, let $H=H^*\\in M_d(\\mathbb C)$ have units joules, let $\\hbar>0$ have units joule-seconds, and let $L_1,\\ldots,L_r\\in M_d(\\mathbb C)$ have units $\\mathrm{s}^{-1/2}$, with the finite GKSL convention of [[def-qsm-dt-gksl-definition]]. Put $K=-iH/\\hbar-\\frac12\\sum_{a=1}^rL_a^*L_a$ and $R(u)=e^{uK}$ for $u\\geq0$, with the exponential defined by its norm-convergent power series. For a density matrix $\\rho\\in M_d(\\mathbb C)$, meaning $\\rho=\\rho^*\\geq0$ and $\\operatorname{Tr}\\rho=1$, define the no-jump branch at time $t\\geq0$ by $W_{\\varnothing,\\varnothing}(t)=R(t)$ and its branch state by $W_{\\varnothing,\\varnothing}(t)\\rho W_{\\varnothing,\\varnothing}(t)^*$.\n\nAll time variables $u,t,s_1,\\ldots,s_n$ are measured in seconds. For $n\\geq1$, a jump-history label is $\\mathbf a=(a_1,\\ldots,a_n)\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}^n$ and its jump times are seconds $0<s_1<\\cdots<s_n<t$. Define the corresponding branch operator by $W_{\\mathbf a,\\mathbf s}(t)=R(t-s_n)L_{a_n}R(s_n-s_{n-1})\\cdots L_{a_2}R(s_2-s_1)L_{a_1}R(s_1)$ and the unnormalized branch state by $W_{\\mathbf a,\\mathbf s}(t)\\rho W_{\\mathbf a,\\mathbf s}(t)^*$. Its branch-weight density is $w_{\\mathbf a,\\mathbf s}(t)=\\operatorname{Tr}(W_{\\mathbf a,\\mathbf s}(t)\\rho W_{\\mathbf a,\\mathbf s}(t)^*)$. The ordered-simplex integral of this density means the repeated Riemann integral $\\int_0^t ds_n\\int_0^{s_n}ds_{n-1}\\cdots\\int_0^{s_2}ds_1$, applied componentwise to matrices; each continuous real component is integrable on the compact integration interval. For $n\\geq1$, $W_{\\mathbf a,\\mathbf s}$ has units $\\mathrm{s}^{-n/2}$ and $w_{\\mathbf a,\\mathbf s}$ has units $\\mathrm{s}^{-n}$; integrating over the $n$ time variables gives a dimensionless weight. If $r=0$, there are no branches with $n\\geq1$. This definition alone does not assert that the branch weights sum to one.",
